The prompt change itself matches #438, but the new regression currently only asserts wording/order in pac-lwot.md. Its test name overstates what it proves.

Add the smallest behavior-oriented regression that actually models the #438 failure shape:
- an authoritative issue contract with concrete requirements/non-goals;
- execution paused on a blocker;
- resume after only the blocker state changes;
- the original contract remains the execution scope without requiring another body fetch;
- a candidate slice with one omitted target requirement and/or one material unrelated addition is surfaced before commit preparation.

Do not add a paid/model E2E or heavyweight workflow simulator unless existing infrastructure requires it. Prefer a small deterministic fixture/test around the existing workflow-routing infrastructure.

Keep the existing prompt-text assertions if useful, but they should complement rather than substitute for the modeled regression.

Re-run npm run check:pi-compatibility.

